(6411008, 949543, 39057, '<td valign="top">I will NOT examine each photo in a challenge to see if I should comment on it or not...DURING THE CHALLENGE...That is insane for you to ask me to do such a thing.<br/> <br/>My god, you''re still trying to change the facts. I commented on your photo DURING the challenge. It is YOU who made a comment in your description that prompted my reply because you put the date and time on the description....ALL POINTING TO MY COMMENT MADE DURING THE CHALLENGE.<br/> <br/>You are the one who should not add sly remarks and not expect a reply. You deleting your comments from your description AFTER I commented is VERY dubious.<br/> <br/><b>I will continue to comment on any photos during any challenges. I can''t help it if yours happens to be one that I comment on. I would suggest that YOU learn to take comments in stride and not moan and call people out by TIMESTAMPING your comments. You should have the guts to comment back DIRECTLY. The sneaky way you commented in your description of your photo and then deleted it was very inflamatory. </b> <br/> <br/>You also say you will ignore my comments....you have said that on more than several occasions....PLEASE DO IT THIS TIME. <br/> <br/>And don''t wish me luck in my activities....it''s just another veiled comment to make you look like the good guy.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i>...very dubious behaviour on Richard''s part. ....</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I highly recommend you boycott my images by never adding comments to my stuff in the future.  There are many other members who would appreciate your focused attention to their photography.  <br/> <br/>The only solution for me is to totally ignore your comments.  You are entitled to your opinions and voting scale.   Good luck in all your activities in the future. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-05-11 15:32:24.</i></td>', 'I will NOT examine each photo in a challenge to see if I should comment on it or not...DURING THE CHALLENGE...That is insane for you to ask me to do such a thing. My god, you''re still trying to change the facts. I commented on your photo DURING the challenge. It is YOU who made a comment in your description that prompted my reply because you put the date and time on the description....ALL POINTING TO MY COMMENT MADE DURING THE CHALLENGE. You are the one who should not add sly remarks and not expect a reply. You deleting your comments from your description AFTER I commented is VERY dubious. I will continue to comment on any photos during any challenges. I can''t help it if yours happens to be one that I comment on. I would suggest that YOU learn to take comments in stride and not moan and call people out by TIMESTAMPING your comments. You should have the guts to comment back DIRECTLY. The sneaky way you commented in your description of your photo and then deleted it was very inflamatory.   You also say you will ignore my comments....you have said that on more than several occasions....PLEASE DO IT THIS TIME.  And don''t wish me luck in my activities....it''s just another veiled comment to make you look like the good guy. Originally posted by hahn23: Originally posted by kenskid:...very dubious behaviour on Richard''s part. .... I highly recommend you boycott my images by never adding comments to my stuff in the future.  There are many other members who would appreciate your focused attention to their photography.   The only solution for me is to totally ignore your comments.  You are entitled to your opinions and voting scale.   Good luck in all your activities in the future. ', '2011-05-11 16:30:23.000000', '2011-05-11 16:32:24.000000', 0),
(6411016, 949702, 96530, '<td valign="top">Love the steam in this- congrats on top twenty Carole!</td>', 'Love the steam in this- congrats on top twenty Carole!', '2011-05-11 16:34:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6411092, 949379, 124256, '<td valign="top">So, as I collect another brown with this one, I get that my post processing made sure the shot did not score well.  As I explained when asked to verify the validity of the shot (I''m not sure why the request was made not that I mind), I was aiming for capturing perhaps something too specific and obscure.  The "bank" or "at least least partially bank owned building" in the shot has obviously seen some wear and tear.  I was thinking that someone financially burdened with this place grabbed their old plastic film camera using expired film, took the shot, and had it processed with the wrong chemicals.  Or something like that.  Anyhow, now that I feel I know how to score a brown, I will start working on a personal best as well, just to broaden the portfolio.  Thank you very much to my commenters!  Oh, and that''s not a fingerprint but just some chickenwire-like fencing stuff -- it extends to the two brown posts to the left.</td>', 'So, as I collect another brown with this one, I get that my post processing made sure the shot did not score well.  As I explained when asked to verify the validity of the shot (I''m not sure why the request was made not that I mind), I was aiming for capturing perhaps something too specific and obscure.  The "bank" or "at least least partially bank owned building" in the shot has obviously seen some wear and tear.  I was thinking that someone financially burdened with this place grabbed their old plastic film camera using expired film, took the shot, and had it processed with the wrong chemicals.  Or something like that.  Anyhow, now that I feel I know how to score a brown, I will start working on a personal best as well, just to broaden the portfolio.  Thank you very much to my commenters!  Oh, and that''s not a fingerprint but just some chickenwire-like fencing stuff -- it extends to the two brown posts to the left.', '2011-05-11 17:44:51.000000', NULL, 0),
