(6412498, 949668, 132177, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DiscoVader:</b></div><hr/><i> I wish the right in the bottom left wasn''t so glaringly bright as I don''t think it should be the focus.  I think I would have cropped it out.  Otherwise I like this shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks a lot for your suggestion. I''m just a rookie and any advise is more then welcome. The photo was shot with an iphone4, but the next one will be with my nikon d50. thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by DiscoVader: I wish the right in the bottom left wasn''t so glaringly bright as I don''t think it should be the focus.  I think I would have cropped it out.  Otherwise I like this shot.   thanks a lot for your suggestion. I''m just a rookie and any advise is more then welcome. The photo was shot with an iphone4, but the next one will be with my nikon d50. thanks again.', '2011-05-13 08:29:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6412499, 949668, 132177, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aylin1478:</b></div><hr/><i> A little grainy </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks a lot for your suggestion. I''m just a rookie and any advise is more then welcome. The photo was shot with an iphone4, but the next one will be with my nikon d50. thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by aylin1478: A little grainy   thanks a lot for your suggestion. I''m just a rookie and any advise is more then welcome. The photo was shot with an iphone4, but the next one will be with my nikon d50. thanks again.', '2011-05-13 08:29:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6412500, 949668, 132177, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by giantmike:</b></div><hr/><i> I see what you were going for here, but there are a couple of things you could do to improve the photo<br/>- There is a lot of noise, so make sure to use a low ISO<br/>- That super bright light near the bottom is pulling the viewer''s eyes. Cropping that out may have helped </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks a lot for your suggestion. I''m just a rookie and any advise is more then welcome. The photo was shot with an iphone4, but the next one will be with my nikon d50. thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by giantmike: I see what you were going for here, but there are a couple of things you could do to improve the photo- There is a lot of noise, so make sure to use a low ISO- That super bright light near the bottom is pulling the viewer''s eyes. Cropping that out may have helped   thanks a lot for your suggestion. I''m just a rookie and any advise is more then welcome. The photo was shot with an iphone4, but the next one will be with my nikon d50. thanks again.', '2011-05-13 08:29:44.000000', NULL, 0),
