(6427049, 949733, 114285, '<td valign="top">He is very cute.</td>', 'He is very cute.', '2011-05-29 02:48:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6428045, 949164, 117474, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MargaretN:</b></div><hr/><i>Does it mean that wide angle lenses are not allowed in Basic? (at least on building shots where the problem is clearly visible) That''s an unusual restriction. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Nah. You just have to live with the distortion in basic. It''s a pain, but it <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=950736" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">can work</a> sometimes (at least I thought it did). <br/> <br/>It probably comes under the "You may not... distort or stretch your image in any way" rule in basic. I know you''re fixing distortion... but technically you''re also distorting the image, I guess. <br/> <br/>Nice image all the same.<br/> <br/>(I know. Random comment. Ignore it!)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-05-30 05:43:45.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by MargaretN:Does it mean that wide angle lenses are not allowed in Basic? (at least on building shots where the problem is clearly visible) That''s an unusual restriction.  Nah. You just have to live with the distortion in basic. It''s a pain, but it can work sometimes (at least I thought it did).  It probably comes under the "You may not... distort or stretch your image in any way" rule in basic. I know you''re fixing distortion... but technically you''re also distorting the image, I guess.  Nice image all the same. (I know. Random comment. Ignore it!)', '2011-05-30 06:43:24.000000', '2011-05-30 06:43:45.000000', 0),
